survey.prompt:
Survey the estate, read-only: ops_inventory validate and list, docker_status, ops_check (include_ok), and prometheus_query count by (job) (up) to see what is scraped; on hosts, host_stats and ssh_exec as the host's read-only account (the default; never as: "operator" - this workflow changes nothing). If the topology tool is available, topology graph (what depends on what, from the inventory, traces and Prometheus). If the grafana tool is available, grafana coverage (inventory services without a dashboard or a Grafana alert rule). Focus: {{input.focus}}

Every tool result ends with an evidence id (ev-xxxxxx): keep the ids with the findings.

Report: the hosts, services, what is monitored and what is not, the dependency graph in short, and anything that looked wrong - short.

report.prompt:
Merge the four analyses in .harness/ops/reports/advisor/ (reliability.md, capacity.md, security.md, cost.md) into one report at .harness/ops/reports/ops-advisor.md: a one-paragraph summary of the estate's state, a table of every recommendation (priority, area, title, effort), then the recommendations in priority order (P1 first), each with Finding, Evidence (keep the exact queries, commands, numbers, evidence ids and links), Impact, Effort, Change and Risk. Drop duplicates; keep every distinct finding. If topology is available, include the dependency graph as a Mermaid block (topology mermaid). Do not change any system.

Specialist summaries: reliability - {{state.reliability}}; capacity - {{state.capacity}}; security - {{state.security}}; cost - {{state.cost}}

Report: the summary paragraph and the P1/P2 titles.
